MethodInstance_GetDefinition_ReturnsMatchingDefinition currently compares only the metadata token (passing a null module out param), so it won't catch regressions in the scope/module resolution. Tokens are only meaningful when paired with the module/scope.

        DacComNullableByRef<IXCLRDataModule> nullModule = new(isNullRef: true);
        uint instanceToken;
        hr = methodInstance.GetTokenAndScope(&instanceToken, nullModule);
        AssertHResult(HResults.S_OK, hr);


src/native/managed/cdac/Microsoft.Diagnostics.DataContractReader.Legacy/ClrDataMethodInstance.cs:80

In DEBUG, ValidateHResult runs whenever _legacyImpl is non-null, but hrLocal is only set when CanFallback() is true. In no-fallback mode this can validate against the default S_OK value and trigger incorrect debug asserts. Gate validation on the same CanFallback() condition used for the legacy call (or track whether the legacy call actually happened).

#if DEBUG
        if (_legacyImpl is not null)
        {
            Debug.ValidateHResult(hr, hrLocal);
        }



